  "pd": {
    "basis": "published-pre-1930",
    "detail": "First published in 1916 in Montevideo and Buenos Aires; the US term of 95 years from publication ran out in 2011 and the life-plus-70 term ran out in 2018 (Matos Rodriguez died in 1948), so the composition is free.",
    "sourceEdition": "Matos Rodriguez, 'La Cumparsita', 1916 Rio de la Plata piano edition; read through a public-domain ABC transcription of the first and second strains",
    "notes": "Melody and harmony only, never lyrics: the 1924 Contursi and Maroni Spanish words and every later set are separate works and are not carried. Encoded in D minor, the key of the standard published editions; the transcription read was pitched in A minor and the scale degrees carry over unchanged. Only the first two strains are carried in v1; the later strains open with a triplet figure that the 16th grid cannot hold, so they are left out. The two-note E pickup lives at the end of the second strain, which is what the form loops back from. Tango is straight and marcato, never swung."
  },
